You are the frontend implementation agent for the DATAra Android application.

PROJECT
- Repository: datara-android
- UI framework: Android Jetpack Compose with Material 3
- Product: DATAra, a mobile-data monitoring and Predicted Exhaustion Time (PET) application
- Current visual identity: dark-only, blue/neon-green accents, data-focused cards, PET-first hierarchy
- Existing screens: Splash, Login, Register, Forgot Password, Dashboard, History and Settings

PRIMARY GOAL
Complete and polish the DATAra frontend through recommended frontend sequence items 1–4.

This is a FRONTEND-ONLY task. Do not implement sequence number 5 or connect the new screens to databases, Room, telemetry, WorkManager, Supabase tables, ONNX models, notification services or real Android permission APIs.

READ BEFORE IMPLEMENTING
1. Read ROADMAP.md.
2. Read AGENTS.md.
3. Inspect the existing Dashboard, History, Settings, Authentication and Navigation code.
4. Inspect design_references only for inspiration. Do not copy the references exactly.
5. Preserve existing user changes and the established DATAra visual identity.

NON-NEGOTIABLE SCOPE
- Use local, in-memory or preview mock state only.
- Do not create repositories, database entities, network requests or fake backend services.
- Do not display mock information as if it were real device data.
- Clearly show “Not connected,” “Unavailable,” “Design preview,” or similar honest states when appropriate.
- Preserve the currently working authentication, session restoration and sign-out behavior.
- Keep the application dark-only. Do not add a theme switch.
- Do not add SMS reading, manual carrier entry, data throttling, address fields or raw device identifiers.
- The secondary phone number remains optional.
- Developer diagnostics must remain hidden behind five taps on the app-version row.
- Prefer existing dependencies and avoid adding libraries solely for visual decoration.

IMPLEMENTATION SEQUENCE

1. FIRST-RUN AND PROMO SETUP SCREENS

Create a Usage Access onboarding flow containing:

- Clear explanation of why DATAra needs usage access.
- Explanation that usage access is special Android access rather than an ordinary permission dialog.
- Short privacy explanation describing what DATAra measures.
- Visible current state such as Not granted, Needs review or Unavailable.
- Primary Continue/Review access action.
- Secondary Not now action.
- Recovery UI for a denied or unavailable state.
- Do not invoke the real Android permission API yet.

Create a Notification Permission introduction screen containing:

- Explanation of PET warnings, consumption milestones and the persistent tracking notification.
- Continue and Not now actions.
- Honest “Not connected in this frontend build” status.
- No real runtime permission request.

Create the Promo Setup flow containing:

- Detected-carrier presentation for Smart, Globe or DITO.
- Carrier-filtered promo catalog using sample data.
- Search or category filtering if it improves usability.
- Selected promo summary.
- Manual promo entry dialog or screen with:
  - Promo name
  - Data allowance in GB
  - Validity in days
  - Expiry date
  - Starting or remaining balance
- Field validation and clear supporting errors.
- A baseline-correction control that lets the user enter the carrier-reported remaining balance.
- A visible disclaimer that DATAra’s balance is an estimate and may differ from the carrier.
- Empty, loading-placeholder, detected-carrier, unavailable-carrier and validation-error designs.
- Do not allow manual carrier entry.

Navigation behavior:

- Successful registration should enter the presentation-only onboarding flow.
- Returning login and restored sessions may continue to Dashboard because real first-run persistence is not available.
- Settings → Usage Access should open the onboarding/review screen.
- Dashboard → Add Promo should open Promo Setup.
- Completing the mock promo flow may update an in-memory UI state, but it must not imply permanent storage.

2. SUPPORTING SCREENS

Create an in-app Notification Center with:

- Header and unread count.
- Empty state.
- Populated sample state.
- Warning categories for PET, 50%/80%/90% consumption and promo expiry.
- Timestamp, title, supporting message and read/unread appearance.
- Local-only Mark as read and Mark all as read interactions.
- Clear distinction between high-priority and informational alerts.
- Dashboard notification bell must open this screen.
- The bell’s unread dot must be state-driven, not always visible.

Create Profile Management with:

- Current name.
- Email displayed as read-only.
- Optional secondary phone number.
- Edit, cancel and local-only save interactions.
- Validation and success feedback.
- No address or device-ID fields.
- Settings → Manage Profile must open this screen.

Create Privacy and Terms screens with:

- Readable sections and headings.
- DATAra-specific explanation of device usage measurement.
- Explanation that device measurements can differ from carrier accounting.
- Explanation of local processing and future synchronization without claiming those systems are currently active.
- Working back navigation.
- Settings links must open the correct screen.

Create a complete hidden Developer Diagnostics screen with:

- Five taps on the Settings app-version row to unlock it.
- Active model mode.
- MAE.
- RMSE.
- R².
- Input tensor summary.
- Inference latency.
- Last prediction time.
- Runtime status.
- Values should show Unavailable in the runtime frontend build.
- Sample values may be used only in Compose previews.
- Do not expose this screen in bottom navigation or normal menus.

3. NAVIGATION AND INTERACTION WIRING

Extend the existing navigation graph for all new destinations.

At minimum, connect:

- Registration success → onboarding.
- Dashboard Add Promo → Promo Setup.
- Dashboard notification bell → Notification Center.
- Settings Manage Profile → Profile.
- Settings Usage Access → Usage Access onboarding.
- Settings System Notification Access → Notification introduction.
- Settings Privacy → Privacy screen.
- Settings Terms → Terms screen.
- Five version taps → Developer Diagnostics.
- Every back button → the expected previous destination.

Top-level navigation must:

- Avoid accumulating duplicate Dashboard, History and Settings destinations.
- Use launchSingleTop, popUpTo, saveState and restoreState appropriately.
- Preserve each top-level destination’s state where practical.
- Keep authenticated screens out of the back stack after sign-out.

No production-visible button should use an unexplained empty callback. If a feature cannot work in this frontend phase, disable it or provide an honest informational message.

4. UI MODERNIZATION, ACCESSIBILITY AND LOCALIZATION

Preserve:

- DATAra’s dark color palette.
- PET-first Dashboard hierarchy.
- Existing brand accents.
- Rounded but restrained cards.
- Floating navigation personality.

Improve:

- Use Scaffold for top-level layouts and navigation instead of repeated fixed bottom padding.
- Use Material 3 components where appropriate:
  - IconButton
  - Button/TextButton
  - NavigationBarItem
  - Switch
  - FilterChip or segmented controls
  - ListItem
  - AlertDialog
- Keep a minimum 48dp touch target.
- Add ripple and pressed feedback.
- Add selected and Role.Tab semantics to navigation.
- Add toggleable Role.Switch semantics to settings rows.
- Add progress semantics to balance and history progress indicators.
- Do not communicate state using color alone.
- Add concise content descriptions to non-decorative icons.
- Avoid duplicate screen-reader announcements.
- Announce important error and success messages using appropriate live-region semantics.
- Ensure layouts remain usable at large font sizes.
- Avoid fixed-width layouts that overflow on narrow phones.
- Make metric layouts responsive:
  - Single-column on compact widths.
  - Two-column or constrained content on expanded widths.
  - Use a navigation rail or suitable adaptive navigation on larger screens if it can be done without unnecessary dependencies.
- Retain edge-to-edge behavior and correctly handle status, navigation and IME insets.
- Use restrained, purposeful animation for state changes; do not add excessive glow or decorative motion.
- Reserve the strongest visual emphasis for PET and primary actions.
- Ensure chart information also has a readable textual summary.

Authentication improvements:

- Change “Forget Password” to “Forgot password?”
- Preserve form values across configuration changes.
- Add Autofill ContentType semantics for name, email, current password and new password.
- Ensure password visibility controls have a proper role, state description and touch target.
- Correct registration button eligibility so the required name field is included.
- Keep field-level validation clear and accessible.

Localization:

- Move all user-visible text from navigable screens into strings.xml.
- Use string resources for labels, errors, descriptions and accessibility text.
- Use formatted strings or plurals for dynamic values.
- Do not concatenate sentences in a way that prevents translation.

STATE REQUIREMENTS

Use explicit UI-state models for all significant screens. Include relevant combinations of:

- Loading
- Empty
- Ready
- Error
- Permission required
- Not connected
- No active promo
- Carrier unavailable
- Tracking stopped
- Offline or stale information
- Read and unread notifications
- View and edit profile modes

Runtime routes should use honest empty/unavailable mock states. Rich sample data should primarily appear in Compose previews.

CONSISTENCY REQUIREMENTS

- Use the same sign-out confirmation behavior everywhere.
- Derive Dashboard insight text from UI state instead of hardcoding “Usage is steady.”
- Derive History trend direction and color from its trend state.
- Derive notification badges from unread state.
- Use consistent headings, spacing, card shapes and button hierarchy.
- Settings toggles may remain local-only, but the UI must not claim they are permanently saved or controlling real alerts.
- Keep cloud sync visibly unavailable until backend integration exists.

DEFINITION OF DONE

The frontend phase is complete when:

- Every required new screen exists and follows DATAra’s visual identity.
- Every visible action navigates, updates local UI state, is disabled, or explains why it is unavailable.
- Dashboard, History and Settings remain operational.
- Authentication and session handling are not broken.
- All new routes have correct back behavior.
- Important empty, loading, ready and unavailable states have previews.
- The layout is usable on compact and expanded widths.
- Core accessibility semantics and touch targets are present.
- User-facing text is stored in resources.
- No database, telemetry, real permission, notification-service, ML or cloud-sync implementation has been introduced.

VERIFICATION CONSTRAINTS

The development computer is resource-limited.

- Do not run clean builds.
- Do not repeatedly run Gradle tasks.
- Do not launch an emulator.
- Do not run ADB installation.
- Do not run full test suites.
- Use Compose previews and careful code inspection first.
- Run at most one lightweight compile check if dependencies are already cached.
- If compilation would require large downloads, stop and report it instead.

FINAL HANDOFF

After implementation, provide:

1. A concise summary of the screens and improvements completed.
2. A list of the principal files created or changed.
3. A clear list of everything that remains mocked or unavailable.
4. Any lightweight verification performed.
5. Do not claim backend or device functionality is working.